                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_59\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes the \"[eXist Home : ...]\" log line in JettyStart.java\nfrom:\n    logger.info(\"[eXist Home : \" + SystemProperties.getInstance().getSystemProperty(\"exist.home\", \"unknown\") + \"]\");\nback to:\n    logger.info(\"[eXist Home : \" + System.getProperty(\"exist.home\", \"unknown\") + \"]\");\n\nThe fix commit message explains why: \"exist.home is not in\nsrc/org/exist/system.properties.\" SystemProperties.getInstance() loads its\nvalues exclusively from a bundled resource file (org/exist/system.properties,\ngenerated at build time with product-version, product-build, svn-revision /\ngit-commit, etc.). exist.home was never one of those generated keys, so any\ncall to SystemProperties.getInstance().getSystemProperty(\"exist.home\", ...)\nis guaranteed to fall through to the default value \"unknown\" \u2014 it can never\nreport the real eXist home directory. The correct source for exist.home is\nthe JVM system property (System.getProperty(\"exist.home\", ...)), which is\nset externally (e.g. via -Dexist.home=... or the launcher script).\n\ncandidate_59 is the commit that introduces this exact bug. It adds the new\nSystemProperties class/mechanism (reading src/org/exist/system.properties)\nand, in the same diff, refactors JettyStart.java's home line:\n    -        msg = \"[eXist Home : \" + System.getProperty(\"exist.home\") + \"]\";\n    +        msg = \"[eXist Home : \" + SystemProperties.getInstance().getSystemProperty(\"exist.home\", \"unknown\") + \"]\";\nThis switches a previously-correct call (System.getProperty, which could\nread the real exist.home JVM property) to the new SystemProperties-backed\nlookup, which never has an \"exist.home\" entry in the properties resource\nfile added by this same commit. From this commit onward, the eXist Home log\nline always prints \"unknown\", regardless of the actual home directory,\nuntil the later fix commit reverts the exist.home lookup to use\nSystem.getProperty directly.\n\nLater candidates (e.g. candidate_66, candidate_69) only reformat or move\nsurrounding code/imports/package (whitespace/brace style, package move to\norg.exist.jetty) but retain the same buggy\nSystemProperties.getInstance().getSystemProperty(\"exist.home\", \"unknown\")\ncall introduced in candidate_59 \u2014 they inherit the bug rather than\nintroduce it. candidate_75 is a near-duplicate of the actual fix diff itself\n(reverting to System.getProperty for exist.home) and is not a\nbug-introducing candidate.\n"
                }
              }
            ]
